      "title": "Conway's Law and Team Topologies",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Conway's Law and Team Topologies",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Conway's Law",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A system's design ==mirrors== the **communication structure** of the org that builds it",
                "{green:Inverse Conway manoeuvre}: shape teams around the target architecture first",
                "The architecture then follows the teams"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Four Team Types",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Team type",
                "Role"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "{blue:Stream-aligned}",
                  "Owns a flow of value"
                ],
                [
                  "{green:Enabling}",
                  "Coaches other teams"
                ],
                [
                  "{purple:Complicated-subsystem}",
                  "Deep specialists"
                ],
                [
                  "{orange:Platform}",
                  "Provides self-service internals"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interaction Modes",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Mode",
                "Nature"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "**Collaboration**",
                  "Temporary, high-bandwidth"
                ],
                [
                  "**X-as-a-Service**",
                  "Clear API, low contact"
                ],
                [
                  "**Facilitating**",
                  "Coach and unblock"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Common Mistake",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Teams split by layer (UI / backend / DB)",
              "text": "Every feature crosses ==three teams== and creates **hand-offs**. Own a slice of value instead."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Service Ownership and Boundaries",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Service Ownership and Boundaries",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. You Build It, You Run It",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==You build it, you run it==: the owning team covers the whole life of its service",
                "==Exactly one== owning team per service",
                "{red:Shared ownership} = **no ownership**"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Design",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Deploy",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "On-call",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Incidents",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Cost",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Artefacts and Load",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Service ==catalogue entry==",
                "==On-call rotation==",
                "==Runbook==",
                "==SLOs==",
                "A ==named contact=="
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Cognitive load: own only what the team can fully ==understand and operate==",
                "Typical limit: ==1-3 services== per team"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Hidden Coupling",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Shared ==database== across teams: a schema change needs cross-team sign-off",
                "Shared ==library== across teams: an upgrade forces coordinated releases"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mistake",
              "text": "Shared database or library = **hidden coupling**. Every change needs ==cross-team coordination==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Monorepo vs Polyrepo",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Monorepo vs Polyrepo",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Two Repo Layouts",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Monorepo",
                "Polyrepo"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Shape",
                  "Many services in ==one repo==",
                  "==One repo== per service"
                ],
                [
                  "Gives",
                  "Atomic cross-service commits, one dependency version set, easy refactors",
                  "Clear ownership, independent access control and release cadence"
                ],
                [
                  "Shared code",
                  "{green:Easy to share}, needs scaling tooling",
                  "{green:Isolated}, risks {red:version drift} of shared libraries"
                ],
                [
                  "Cross-service change",
                  "One commit",
                  "Coordinated PRs across repos"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Monorepo Tooling",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==CODEOWNERS== gives per-path review: each folder has its owning team",
                "==Affected-only builds==: build and test just what a change touches",
                "Tools: **Bazel**, **Nx**, **Turborepo**"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "text",
              "lines": [
                "/services/orders/  @acme/orders-team",
                "/libs/auth/        @acme/platform-team"
              ],
              "note": "CODEOWNERS: path, then owning team"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Monorepo without ==path-based CI==: every change runs every build",
                "Polyrepo without ==shared-library versioning==: services drift apart"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Pick by trade-off",
              "text": "Monorepo = ==share and change together==, but invest in tooling. Polyrepo = ==isolate==, but version shared libraries."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Independent Pipelines per Service",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Independent Pipelines per Service",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. One Pipeline per Service",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Each service has its ==own build, test, deploy== pipeline",
                "A service can {green:ship alone}, without releasing the others",
                "Monorepo trigger: ==path filters==, so only the changed service builds"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "yaml",
              "lines": [
                "on:",
                "  push:",
                "    paths: ['services/orders/**']"
              ],
              "note": "GitHub Actions: runs only when orders changes"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Safe Independent Deploys",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Needs ==backward-compatible APIs==, so old consumers keep working",
                "Add ==contract tests== (e.g. Pact) so consumers don't break",
                "Use **immutable artefacts**: one image tag per ==commit SHA=="
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Commit",
                    "sub": "SHA abc123",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Build image",
                    "sub": "tag = SHA",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Staging",
                    "sub": "same artefact",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Prod",
                    "sub": "same artefact",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A ==lockstep release train== forces services to deploy together",
                "One ==shared pipeline== for all services does the same",
                "Result: a {red:distributed monolith}"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "text": "Why can one service deploy alone? **Own pipeline**, compatible APIs, contract tests. Same SHA-tagged artefact goes staging to prod."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
